  "chapter": {
    "number": 20,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(21) For the end, a Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord, the king shall rejoice in your strength; and in your salvation he shall greatly exult.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have granted him the desire of his soul, and have not withheld from him the request of his lips. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you have prevented him with blessings of goodness: you have set upon his head a crown of precious stone.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He asked life of you, and you gave him length of days for ever and ever.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "His glory is great in your salvation: you will crown him with glory and majesty.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you will give him a blessing for ever and ever: you will gladden him with joy with your countenance.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the king trusts in the Lord, and through the mercy of the Highest he shall not be moved.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let your hand be found by all your enemies: let your right hand find all that hate you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You shall make them as a fiery oven at the time of your presence: the Lord shall trouble them in his anger, and fire shall devour them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You shall destroy their fruit from the earth, and their seed from among the sons of men.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For they intended evils against you; they imagined a device which they shall by no means be able to perform.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For you shall make them turn their back in your latter end, you will prepare their face.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Be you exalted, O Lord, in your strength: we will sing and praise your mighty acts.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": []
  },
